# Env for the crush-signal harness (referenced as env_file in harness.toml).
#
# harness parses this as KEY=VALUE (a leading `export ` and surrounding quotes are
# tolerated) and layers it ON TOP of the daemon's own environment — spawn.go does
# `env := os.Environ()` and appends, so PATH and everything else the daemon already
# has still reaches crush; these entries just win on conflict.
#
# NO SECRETS HERE. This file is committed to the dotfiles repo. Crush's provider key
# ($ZAI_API_TOKEN) and every MCP token come from ~/.config/vault/secrets-static.env,
# which Vault Agent renders from OpenBao. The daemon's own supervision carries them:
# harness.service loads the systemd-syntax copy via EnvironmentFile, and the
# rocks.stump.harness LaunchAgent sources secrets-static.env before exec — so this
# harness inherits every secret from the daemon, and this file stays knobs-only.
# Running `harness daemon` by hand? Source secrets-static.env first (a login shell
# already has, via ~/.oh-my-zsh/custom/00-secrets.zsh).

# Repoint crush's override config (GlobalConfigData) at a per-harness file, so the
# model pin in ~/.local/share/crush-signal/crush.json applies to this supervised
# crush and not to the one you run by hand. Unset, this would be
# ~/.local/share/crush. The dir also holds this agent's session history, so if you
# rename the harness again, `mv` the dir rather than letting a new one be seeded.
CRUSH_GLOBAL_DATA={{ .chezmoi.homeDir }}/.local/share/crush-signal

{{ $user := .agentIdentity | default .chezmoi.username -}}
{{ $role := hasSuffix "-agent" $user | ternary "agent" "human" -}}
# SIGNAL_MCP_PREFIX is IDENTITY-CONDITIONAL, on the same $USER / $USER-agent
# convention every other agent template uses (.chezmoidata.yaml § Identity,
# dot_config/crush/CRUSH.md.tmpl): a login carrying the `-agent` suffix is the
# bot, anything else is the human. The two deployments want opposite answers.
#
#   human login (joestump, e.g. kitt) — the Signal account is Joe's OWN, and its
#     Note to Self also carries #todo / #bookmark / #journal items belonging to
#     other automations. This agent must take only what is addressed to it, so
#     it keeps the `cc` prefix: "cc deploy" and "cc: deploy" match on a word
#     boundary, "ccdeploy" does not, and the prefix is stripped before delivery.
#
#   agent login (joestump-agent, e.g. tars) — the Signal account IS the agent's.
#     Every trusted-sender message (Joe, Chelsea, Jon) is meant for it, so it
#     takes NO prefix and the key is omitted entirely below.
#
# This split is the bug being fixed: BOTH boxes shipped SIGNAL_MCP_PREFIX=cc, so
# messaging joestump-agent@ without a prefix got silence — from an agent that was
# `running` in `harness list` with zero restarts and a clean `harness doctor`.
#
# Omitted, not empty, on the agent side. signal-mcp treats unset and empty
# identically (`os.environ.get("SIGNAL_MCP_PREFIX", "")` then `if config.prefix:`
# in signal_mcp/channel.py), but harness appends this file LAST when composing
# the child env and later duplicates shadow earlier ones (internal/supervisor/
# spawn.go buildEnv) — so ANY line here, even an empty one, permanently shadows
# whatever Vault Agent renders from OpenBao. Omitting it is what leaves
# secret/users/<whoami>/signal able to set a prefix later; setting it empty is
# what made the OpenBao override look broken.
{{ if ne $role "agent" -}}
SIGNAL_MCP_PREFIX=cc
{{ end -}}
